te"><addressbook><name>SHIMAMURA, HARUNARI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A non-aqueous electrolyte secondary cell having an excellent capacity maintaining rate in charging/discharging cycles. The charging/discharging cycle characteristics are improved, and the initial charging capacity is excellent. The cell includes a negative plate, a positive plate, and a non-aqueous electrolyte. The negative plate contains an alloy containing Si, a first element, and a second element. The first element is at least one selected from a group of the Group 2 elements except Mg, the transition elements, the Group 12 elements, the Group 13 elements except B, and the Group 14 elements except Si in the periodic table. The second element is at least one of B and Mg.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une cellule secondaire à électrolyte non aqueux qui a un excellent taux de maintien de capacité dans les cycles de charge/décharge. Les caractéristiques de ces cycles sont améliorées, et la capacité de charge initiale est excellente. La cellule comprend une plaque négative, une plaque positive et un électrolyte non aqueux. La plaque négative renferme un alliage à base de Si, un premier élément et un second élément. Le premier élément appartient au moins aux éléments du groupe 2, à l'exception de Mg, aux éléments de transition, aux éléments du groupe 12, aux éléments du groupe 13, à l'exception de B, et aux éléments du groupe 14, à l'exception de Si, dans le tableau périodique des éléments. Le second élément est au moins B ou Mg.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>